Specifically, the message framing (F0 42 3g 00 01 <id> <msgId> ... F7), the
message-ID table, the acknowledgement codes (ht_sysex_format) and the pattern
dump/write byte order (e2pat2syx.py) follow that implementation.

The NRPN layer (hacktribeNrpn.ts) follows utils/ht_nrpn_format.py and the
hacktribe wiki MIDI.md; the FX type and parameter tables (e2FxParams.ts) follow
utils/ht_fx_ram_format.py and utils/ht_fx_preset_format.py. Both were taken via
Synthstudio, which ported them from the same source. The RAM peek/poke layer
(hacktribeRam.ts) follows utils/ht_sysex.py; its address map is documented in
omnitribe/docs/reverse/hacktribe_ram_and_formats.md.

The FX preset layout (e2FxPreset.ts) — the 0x20C-byte block with name, control
map, and the IFX 1 / IFX 2 / MFX chain stages — is ported directly from
utils/ht_fx_preset_format.py of the same project (cloned 2026-08-25). The
write-side slot limits (IFX < 96, MFX < 32) follow utils/ht_sysex.py; the fork
at https://github.com/13HansSeppaufpepp12/hacktribe-editor (e2_formats.py) was
consulted for the groove-template layout and confirms the same FX structure.

The groove-template layout (e2Groove.ts) — the 0x140-byte block with GVST/GVED
markers, name, length and 64 four-byte steps — is ported from
extra/e2_groove_template.py of the same project, including its value ranges
(trigger ±0x30 two's complement, velocity 0..0x7F, gate 0..0x60). Note that the
fork's e2_formats.py places the step table at 0x24 while the upstream tool uses
0x30; TekkForge follows the upstream tool and verifies the 0xFF step marker at
read time.

